# Keep the build context to what `cargo build --release` actually reads
# (`Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `src/`, `templates/`). Everything else only
# slows the upload and busts the dependency-cache layer.
#
# Patterns without a slash match at the context root only, so `*.html` and
# `*.md` do not reach into `templates/` or `doc/` — `templates/report.html` is
# still sent and the build needs it. Use `**/` for a recursive match.

# Rust build output and local caches
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore

# CI definitions (not needed to compile)
.github/

# Documentation, knowledge base and agent tooling
doc/
docs/
.claude/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Local agent scratch space (work journals)
tmp/

# Generated reports and local HTML output
*.html

# Markdown (README, licenses are copied only by the release workflow)
*.md

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
